{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A parking lot has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> more cars than trucks. The ratio of cars to trucks is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b72b5a287005d244507327fdfbed31e333415fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 : 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 4 : 1 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 9 : 5\\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 5 : 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 3 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"509\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of trucks, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of cars. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> more cars than trucks, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/4263b2df3e167e5ff745753bf1dd01b42b6073b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 0.25t + 1.00t = 1.25t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of cars to trucks is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/7317da88900dc7f4d38bce0695316c51b993e189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c : t = 1.25t : t = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 5 : 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"221\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can pick an easy number to find the ratio with. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of trucks, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of cars. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> more cars than trucks, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c043fc27290e57636c4bcc7cc3544f2b7335628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 0.25 \\times 4 + 1.00 \\times 4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of cars to trucks is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d1163ac9ffea61a8e2ae96d6851b2e274547dbbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c : 4 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 5 : 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 